    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n61336" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κώνει-ον</span></b> , τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>hemlock, Conium maculatum</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Steril.</u>
				224
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				1.5.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				9.8.3
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Al.</u>
				186
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				4.78
			</span></i>, etc. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νάρθηξ</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Iamb.</u>
				1.122
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>hemlockjuice</i>, poison by which criminals were put to death
			at Athens, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				124
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κώνειον πεπωκώς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ly.</u>
					219e
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ κώνειον ἔπιεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>HG</u>
					2.3.56
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				And.
				3.10
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κώνεια πιεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Ra.</u>
					1051
				</span></i>
			.</div>
